s is upf 50 and  it's made from like a stretchy nylon  elastane so rashfests are meant to be  worn while you're swimming and so you  don't have to worry as much about all  the sunscreen coming off in the water  you only have to reapply to a much more  limited area  and of course the worst thing is trying  to apply sunscreen to your back and of  course this covers your back  when i was talking about upf protective  clothing a lot of my followers suggested  solbari to me and i'm actually wearing a  solbari shirt now  this one so barry actually sent me a few  items of their clothing to look at  when i asked them about the technology  they used in their clothes  mecca also sent me the rashvest for a  different thing so the thing i really  like about solbari is that they have  really nice  fashionable designs that look like  normal clothes  some of their clothing is probably a bit  more like avant-garde  it really depends on what you're  comfortable wearing although now i think  maybe masks are a lot more acceptable  so we've sold barry's clothes as well as  the fabrics that they use that are  really high uv protection  they also have design aspects of their  clothes as well which help protect you  from the sun  so for example a lot of their clothes  have these thumb holes which means that  you can put them like this and that  protects the back of your hands  a lot of their clothes also fit really  tightly around your neck or  they can even go up above your neck and  so that gives you more neck protection  because that is a really common place to  get burnt  so barry have a bunch of different  fabrics with different technologies in  them  so some of them are more breathable some  of them are moisture wicking  some of them are cooling and there's  also ones which are anti-odor  there's a sensitive range which is  really good if you have sensitive skin  that's also sun sensitive  these are a blend of organic cotton and  bamboo and they have a really high upf  but they're a